WEBVTT

00:05.550 --> 00:10.920
We've talked a little bit already about project management offices and how they can help or support

00:11.070 --> 00:12.400
the project manager.

00:12.510 --> 00:16.170
But there are some more characteristics you need to know for your exam.

00:16.380 --> 00:22.750
The project management office is a uniform approach for project management in that organization.

00:22.820 --> 00:26.110
And remember PMO can exist in the whole organization.

00:26.130 --> 00:32.850
A department of lines of business but a PMO is generally there has some control over the projects within

00:32.850 --> 00:33.720
that domain.

00:33.720 --> 00:39.630
Whether it's the whole company or organization or different departments or lines of business the goal

00:39.630 --> 00:45.140
is to surprise support not surprise that's going to support the project manager.

00:45.210 --> 00:52.890
The PMO provides organizational process assets so templates formed software things that help the project

00:52.890 --> 00:55.780
manager do their job.

00:55.800 --> 01:02.000
There are some different types of those though you want to be familiar with the first one is a directive.

01:02.010 --> 01:08.990
PMO directive PMO is where the project manager is really part of the PMO.

01:09.060 --> 01:13.200
The PMO manages and controls all projects.

01:13.200 --> 01:15.650
So the PMO control is very high.

01:15.660 --> 01:22.170
The PM is part of the PMO and our organisation wants to do a project or a team wants to do a project

01:22.170 --> 01:24.010
or a stakeholder wants to do a project.

01:24.060 --> 01:28.470
They give that project to the PMO and the PMO controls it.

01:28.470 --> 01:34.200
That they have a uniform approach and they do everything as far as project management goes with all

01:34.200 --> 01:37.140
projects in that organization.

01:37.140 --> 01:44.970
Then we have what's called a controlling PMO the controlling PMO defines project governance that they

01:44.970 --> 01:50.100
set up what the governance will be for projects so they kind of create the framework and give it to

01:50.100 --> 01:55.300
the project managers where the PM isn't necessarily part of the PMO.

01:55.410 --> 01:59.040
They have required templates and forms and oversight.

01:59.040 --> 02:02.030
They define what the project management activities are.

02:02.070 --> 02:07.440
They set communication requirements and so the PMO control is considered moderate.

02:07.440 --> 02:13.580
It's like they give the framework and the structure to the project manager and so there is some oversight

02:13.860 --> 02:20.620
but they're definitely not as controlling as we saw in the directive.

02:20.820 --> 02:28.950
The next PMO is supporting a support PMO is where the PMO acts as a coach or a consultant and they can

02:28.950 --> 02:34.890
help the project manager but they don't really control the project manager so they're more of a consultation

02:34.900 --> 02:35.450
role.

02:35.550 --> 02:41.850
So they're giving advice and forms and software of best practices but they're not really telling the

02:41.850 --> 02:44.320
PM how to do the work.

02:44.400 --> 02:49.980
So you have directive with the most control we have controlling but just a little bit less it's a little

02:49.980 --> 02:56.150
bit more moderate control and then very low and control is the support of PMO.

02:56.160 --> 03:01.590
All right so no those stereotypes appear most just as if you know the organisation types keep moving

03:01.590 --> 03:02.280
forward.
